{"id": "9b0aad1e9803727a", "facts": [
{"fact": "0.0", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "In the light - dependent reactions ( mainly three vital reaction steps"}]},
{"fact": "0.1", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "( I ) Hill and Bendall 's Z - scheme of cyclic and non-cyclic reactions"}]},
{"fact": "0.2", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "( II ) Mitchell 's chemi - osmosis for ATP synthesis"}]},
{"fact": "0.3", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "( III ) Dolai 's S - state diagrams in water - splitting"}]},
{"fact": "0.4", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "one molecule of the pigment chlorophyll absorbs one photon"}]},
{"fact": "0.5", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "one molecule of the pigment chlorophyll absorbs one photon and loses one electron"}]},
{"fact": "0.6", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "This electron is passed to a modified form of chlorophyll called pheophytin"}]},
{"fact": "0.7", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "which passes the electron to a quinone molecule"}]},
{"fact": "0.8", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "starting the flow of electrons down an electron transport chain"}]},
{"fact": "0.9", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "electron transport chain that leads to the ultimate reduction of NADP to NADPH"}]},
{"fact": "0.10", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "In addition , this creates a proton gradient ( energy gradient ) across the chloroplast membrane"}]},
{"fact": "0.11", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "which is used by ATP synthase in the synthesis of ATP"}]},
{"fact": "0.12", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "The chlorophyll molecule ultimately regains the electron it lost"}]},
{"fact": "0.13", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "regains the electron it lost when a water molecule is split in a process called photolysis"}]},
{"fact": "0.14", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 5, "quote": "which releases a dioxygen ( O ) molecule as a waste product"}]},
{"fact": "1.0", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "Although photosynthesis is performed differently by different species"}]},
{"fact": "1.1", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "the process always begins when energy from light is absorbed by proteins called reaction centres"}]},
{"fact": "1.2", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "proteins called reaction centres that contain green chlorophyll pigments"}]},
{"fact": "1.3", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "In plants , these proteins are held inside organelles called chloroplasts"}]},
{"fact": "1.4", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "organelles called chloroplasts , which are most abundant in leaf cells"}]},
{"fact": "1.5", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "while in bacteria they are embedded in the plasma membrane"}]},
{"fact": "1.6", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "In these light - dependent reactions , some energy is used to strip electrons from suitable substances , such as water"}]},
{"fact": "1.7", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "some energy is used to strip electrons from suitable substances , such as water , producing oxygen gas"}]},
{"fact": "1.8", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "The hydrogen freed by the splitting of water is used in the creation of two further compounds"}]},
{"fact": "1.9", "status": "stated", "evidence": [{"item": 6, "quote": "two further compounds that act as an immediate energy storage means"}]},
